{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":31118,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"85ccf62633f42e62f588b3fb5c5b9874b1912aca6dbb76d121f2d922345a2314","packTokens":17644,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":1,"sections":[{"id":"side","tokens":100,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":372,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"standard-topics","tokens":249,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":79,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":3730,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sketches","tokens":5070,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"differences","tokens":2240,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"request","tokens":5707,"trimmed":false,"trust":"untrusted"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"clarifier"},"pointers":[],"system":"PRODUCT SIDE. This run builds the API side of the product these requirements describe, in an existing .NET API project: every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there, and the data behind them. The web app is built in its own repo: no screen is built here, and no criterion is written for one.\n\nRequirements analyst. Your only job is finding what is unclear or missing. You don't write the spec.\nCheck: scope, data model, user roles and permissions, existing data and state changes, error and failure handling, external systems, hardcoded identifiers (constant or configuration?), behaviour outside the named scope, terminology.\nFor each issue: a question with 2-4 options, one \"recommended\" (copy the option text exactly) with a one-line reason, the intent spans it affects, impact 1-3 with a reason (3 = changes data or who sees what: writes, orders, permissions, money; 2 = a visible flow; 1 = wording). If it comes from a listed disagreement, give its id in \"difference\".\nThe recommended option is always the smallest change that fully does what the request asks. Never recommend